Turn startup auto-apply on?

Every L-Mechrevo start would really write the values listed under "Will write" below into the SMU (not a read-only check; where this machine cannot write FMax, FMax is neither listed nor written). A bad value can freeze or restart the PC.

Will write: {0}
Current baseline (read when the window opened): {1}

It lasts for this boot only, the firmware starts over after a reboot. Continue?

Reset writes 0 to every core and then sends one all-core CO 0 fallback, and it exits fixed-clock mode.

It clears every core, including offsets that already existed before you opened this window, plus the saved per-core values (so startup auto-apply cannot replay what you just cleared).

Where the machine supports writing FMax, Reset also puts FMax back to the baseline that was read last time; if no baseline was recorded, no FMax value is guessed and none is written.

